fun main() { var x = 1; { var x = 2; x = 5; print x; } print x; }
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// w04_shadow_assign.mini - my own example: an assignment inside a block
// changes only the inner x.
//
// Prediction: the inner var x gets ID 1, and x = 5 looks x up in the inner map,
// so it also uses ID 1. The outer x (ID 0) is never touched.
//
// Try:  minic run w04/w04_shadow_assign.mini   -> 5
//                                                  1
// Compare w04_outer.mini: without the inner var, x = 30 fails, because the
// block's map has no x.
